'''vomitingly''' (vom′i-ting-li), ''adv.'' As in vor ing; like vomit.
{{smaller block|Take occasion, pulling out your gloves, to have s epigram, or satire, or sonnet fastened in one of them, may, as it were ''vomitingly'' to you, offer itself to the ge men. {{right|''Dekker'', Gull’s Hornbook, p.}}}}

